# issue #2381: pre-#2348 flat hook-fires counter. Issue #2348 replaced it
# with per-session shards under .orchestrate-hook-fires/ (hook_fires.py /
# on-the-record/hooks/hook-fires.sh) specifically to stop every session's
# local edits to this one shared tracked path from diverging local main
# from origin/main. Nothing writes this exact filename anymore; ignored
# so no stray pre-#2348 branch/script can reintroduce that drift.
.orchestrate-hook-fires.log
# issue #2381 (round 2): the sharding in #2348 moved the divergence, it
# didn't remove it — every session still committed its own shard under
# this directory, which is exactly the mechanical cause tracked in issue
# #2506. hook_fires.py's own _hook_fires_aggregate() only ever globs this
# directory under the session's local workspace (never the shared
# on-the-record checkout, per its docstring) and nothing reads a
# committed copy across sessions, so untracking it drops no observability
# — the shards are still written to and read from disk exactly as today.
.orchestrate-hook-fires/
